2026-09-24  Alexander Karlberg  <alexander.karlberg@mpp.mpg.de>

	* src/matrix_element_dihiggs.f90 (eval_matrix_element_tensor):
	Fixed the F3 terms of the tensor matrix element. The four-vectors
	were stored with their contravariant components in tensors declared
	with lower indices, i.e. as the parity-flipped vectors, while the
	Levi-Civita tensor of the F3 part of the hadronic tensor was not
	flipped. This gave wrong F3 x F3 interference terms between the
	g^mu_nu and the t/u-channel parts of the VV -> HH current (about
	1e-4 of the cross section; the F1 and F2 terms were not affected).
	The vectors are now lowered with the metric. With zero widths the
	tensor and the analytic (default) matrix element now agree to
	machine precision, F3 included. The analytic F3F3 expression in
	ME_expressions.f was correct.

	* src/tensor.f90:
	* tests/test_tensor.f90:
	Added InitFourVector(tensor, p, up), which stores a four-vector
	given by its contravariant components with its index up or down
	(lowering it with the metric).

	* src/tensor.f90:
	Rewritten without allocatable components (fixed-size arrays, no
	deep copies), about twice as fast; same interface, and the same
	results to the last bit. Fixed the rank-2 x rank-1 contraction over
	the second index (not used by the matrix elements). The same file is
	now used in proVBFH, proVBFHH and proVBFH-inclusive.

	* tests/{tensor_legacy.f90|test_tensor.f90}:
	* Makefile:
	Added "make check": unit test of src/tensor.f90 against the previous
	implementation (kept as tests/tensor_legacy.f90) and against
	explicit formulae, on random inputs.

